Z||000000||RobertVol||02-10-2000||01:13 AM||||Just wondering can anybody tell me is there anyone near the Jax,FL  area that works on fieros? I will be doing some major engine and drivetrain mods over the next few months. But I do not want some idiot working on my baby. And I dont want to drive hundreds of miles unless I have to. THANKS! ||||reg||10
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-10-2000||08:11 AM||||I'm sure there is someone that maybe closer. But the shop that did all the work to my car is here in Atlanta. Few hour drive for you though. But if you have it done right the first time you'll never have to do it again... there is a picture of a motor that the guy didn't do it right the first time... now the shop is doing it for him. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net/gsr.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net/gsr.htm</A>   see my car at... <A HREF="http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html</A>   or the shop at... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||02-10-2000||09:51 AM||||I just moved out of J-ville last year, and I never really heard of any shops per say that did custom work on Fieros.  Although I ran into a guy in the Pep Boys on Dunn Ave (northside) that had a V8 GT.  You might try giving the "Supershops" store on Blanding Blvd a call, some of the guys in there may know of people who do custom work.  I know there use to be gatherings at Supershops on Saturday evenings, but I dont recall ever seeing any Fieros there.  Also, there was a guy that worked at the Ponitac dealership at the corner of Atlantic and Southside.  He had a nice GT. <P>Hope this helps...Good Luck<P>BTW, where in/near Jax are you?||||reg||1
Z||000003||RobertVol||02-10-2000||08:21 PM||||Southside area. Near the Avenues. Thanks for the info. I gues I may have to go out of state..||||reg||2
